From ddce0e6ba2d3498f63b31623fe856b9667a9fbb9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lina <lokinyauv@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 4 Aug 2026 03:59:14 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] fix: release base stations while sitting in the tray

With "Allow tray" on, the close button hides the window instead of
quitting, so the process keeps running - and kept holding every base
station. A station only accepts one connection at a time, so a second
machine could never connect while the app sat in the tray. From the
user's side it looks like they quit the app but the stations stay
locked, with no way to hand them over short of killing the process.

Hiding to tray now drops the links, and they're re-established when
the window comes back (tray "Show", a second launch) or when a power
command needs them - ChangeBaseStationPowerStatus reconnects on
demand, so the SteamVR automation still works from the tray. A
background watcher covers the remaining case: once SteamVR exits and
the stations have been put to sleep, the now-idle links are dropped
too.

Links are kept, not dropped, when the window hides while a VR session
is already running - that machine is actively using them.

(cherry picked from commit 40b49048ba55dce244675261572cd63c912aa322)
