From d6c744e1765fbec8bc58df36d6444e9f5254761b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lina <lokinyauv@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 10 Aug 2026 14:56:12 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] feat: quit once SteamVR exits and the stations are asleep

With SteamVR auto-launching the app there is no reason for it to stay
resident after the session ends - it just sits in the tray holding the
base stations. Shut down instead once the session is over.

Order matters: this runs after the sleep commands have finished rather
than on the SteamVR event itself, because exiting first would cut them
off halfway and leave the stations awake.

Quitting can't be undone, so the SteamVR state is re-checked against
the process directly before pulling the trigger - putting stations to
sleep takes long enough that a new session may already have started.

Only applies when "manage power based on SteamVR" is on, and only on a
real running -> stopped transition, so starting the app by hand with no
SteamVR around leaves it alone.

(cherry picked from commit 6afec4cc06481b48e7eee4632fe71fb2d7f97b4a)
