From ffc2e4ad29edb3ecd600892529c9de688f05a751 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lina <lokinyauv@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 12 Aug 2026 07:47:52 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] fix: keep the BLE links instead of releasing them while
 idle in the tray

Releasing the stations mid-life poisons the process. tinygo's Windows
Disconnect returns early when closing the GATT session fails:

	if err := d.session.Close(); err != nil {
		return err          // d.device.Close() below never runs
	}

so BluetoothLEDevice.Close() is skipped and Windows keeps a half-open
handle. Every connect afterwards still finds the service but comes
back with an empty characteristic list.

The log shows it exactly. Both stations connected at 21:48 and worked
all night; at 07:26 the idle timer fired, the disconnect failed with
"Incorrect function", and from that point every single attempt logged
"Mode: false, Power: false, ID: false" - 39 of them, against two
successes for the whole run. A fresh process always worked, which is
why restarting the app kept appearing to fix it.

Releasing existed so a station wouldn't sit claimed and unusable from
another machine. That's covered better now: the app quits when SteamVR
exits, which hands them back for real, and a process on its way out
can't be poisoned by a failed disconnect. So keep the links while
running and leave the disconnects on the exit paths only.

Verified: over a minute idle in the tray with SteamVR closed, zero
disconnects, zero "Mode: false", both stations still ready.

(cherry picked from commit ecce72859b3a17666aa573bffcd16f9dfcf3a795)
